    "6:00 am in inn: Rita reaches the square. Phil says: Morning, Rita. I'm still in the lobby. I need to get to the studio for the seven o'clock bulletin. I'm riding the one o'clock coach out to Pittsburgh, so I don't have time for the square today. I'll be back on Wednesday to help move that couch. Phil spends the period at the inn. You see Larry at the square.",
    "9:30 am in square: Rita inspects the square. The band is setting up. Larry says: Rita, the bandstand is over there. I'm scanning for a wide before they start tuning. Larry looks around.",
    "1:00 pm in square: Rita stays for the band's cornet solo. Larry says: This is a beautiful piece, isn't it? I'm so sorry, but I have to let you down. I used my only charged battery this morning filming the general festival atmosphere. I have no power left to shoot the band or that cornet solo I wanted to do. I'll stay here to listen and keep an eye out for any other opportunities, but I can't give you the specific footage you wanted from this performance. Larry stays for the band's cornet solo. Rita invites Larry on the crew radio to contribute to the evening slot."
